# Publish Model

## Purpose

Define the canonical publish-ready schema for the reporting client before wiring:

- export sync
- normalization
- LLM text generation
- MkDocs page rendering

This is the contract between the local content pipeline and the docs renderer.

The flow is:

```text
raw export payload -> normalized factual model -> generated publish model -> Markdown -> MkDocs site
```

The docs layer must consume only the publish model.

## Design Rules

1. The publish model is page-oriented, not export-oriented.
2. Factual fields and generated fields are stored separately.
3. Generated text must be replaceable without changing page templates.
4. Placeholder text is allowed in v0 so layout can be built before live generation.
5. Completed jobs are the default publication source.

## Page Types

Three page types are required:

- `home`
- `project`
- `tree`

## Common Conventions

- IDs are stable strings.
- Paths are repo-relative publish paths.
- Image paths are site-relative asset paths.
- GeoJSON paths are downloadable artifact paths.
- Generated fields may contain placeholder text in the form `FUNCTION: ...`.

## Layout Regions

Every rendered page should reserve layout space for:

- global header
- global navigation bar
- main content body
- map region when map content exists
- image gallery region when image content exists
- global footer

These regions should be represented in the publish model so the template layer
does not need to guess where content belongs.

Recommended site-wide layout blocks:

```json
{
  "layout": {
    "header": {
      "site_title": "Urban Forestry Assessment Report",
      "project_tagline": "Static reporting site for completed field assessments",
      "logo_path": "assets/branding/logo.png"
    },
    "navbar": [
      { "label": "Home", "path": "index.md" },
      { "label": "Projects", "path": "projects/index.md" },
      { "label": "Maps", "path": "maps/index.md" }
    ],
    "footer": {
      "organization_name": "An Arborist",
      "published_text": "Published from local reporting artifacts",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-25T00:00:00Z"
    }
  }
}
```

## Home Schema

```json
{
  "page_type": "home",
  "site_title": "Urban Forestry Assessment Report",
  "layout": {
    "header": {
      "site_title": "Urban Forestry Assessment Report",
      "project_tagline": "Static reporting site for completed field assessments",
      "logo_path": "assets/branding/logo.png"
    },
    "navbar": [
      { "label": "Home", "path": "index.md" },
      { "label": "Projects", "path": "projects/index.md" },
      { "label": "Maps", "path": "maps/index.md" }
    ],
    "footer": {
      "organization_name": "An Arborist",
      "published_text": "Published from local reporting artifacts",
      "updated_at": "2026-03-25T00:00:00Z"
    }
  },
  "site_intro": "FUNCTION: generate_home_intro(site_summary)",
  "summary": {
    "assessment_count": 0,
    "tree_count": 0,
    "species_count": 0,
    "project_count": 0,
    "risk_counts": {
      "low": 0,
      "moderate": 0,
      "high": 0,
      "extreme": 0
    }
  },
  "combined_map": {
    "image_path": "assets/maps/all-projects-overview.svg",
    "alt": "Combined map showing all assessed trees colored by project"
  },
  "featured_images": [
    {
      "image_path": "assets/images/home/hero_project_alpha.jpg",
      "caption": "Project Alpha overview"
    },
    {
      "image_path": "assets/images/home/hero_project_bravo.jpg",
      "caption": "Project Bravo overview"
    }
  ],
  "projects": [
    {
      "project_id": "project_alpha",
      "project_name": "Project Alpha",
      "theme_color": "#2F6B4F",
      "project_path": "projects/project_alpha.md",
      "area_map_path": "assets/maps/project_alpha_overview.svg",
      "area_description": "FUNCTION: generate_project_area_description(project_alpha)",
      "assessment_count": 0,
      "species_count": 0
    }
  ]
}
```

